Licensing map
=============

This repository contains two kinds of material, under two licences. Which
applies depends on the directory, because part of the work is original and part
of it is a modification of someone else's project.

MIT (see LICENSE)
-----------------
  docs/      notes/      scripts/      tests/      tools/

  Original work: the debugging and automation tooling, the test suites, the
  build and launch scripts, and the written notes. Reuse, modify and fork
  freely; attribution is the only condition.

LGPL-2.1-or-later (see LICENSE.LGPL-2.1)
----------------------------------------
  patches/

  These are modifications to Wine and to Proton, distributed as plain git
  diffs. Wine is LGPL-2.1-or-later, so a modification of it is too, and it
  stays that way however it is redistributed. If you ship binaries built from
  these patches you must also make the corresponding source available, as the
  LGPL requires.

  Note that tests/ and tools/ include a few Wine headers when they are built.
  That does not change their licence, but it does mean you need a Wine source
  tree to build them.

